Interpret spectral shape lines and shifts with competing physical explanations (@physics-astronomy-spectra: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Connect-orbital-and-transit-evidence-to-planetary-systems.lingua#r_0061F9B72C184476321D5F90D0") { r_0021544784FC107EAF259C12AC
A spectrum records a distribution over wavelength or frequency after instrument response and propagation. The two densities satisfy F_ν dν=−F_λ dλ in oriented differentials, or F_ν=F_λ λ²/c when using positive bin widths. A peak of F_λ and a peak of F_ν do not generally correspond by simply replacing λ with c/ν. Color is a ratio or magnitude difference between specified bands, not an intrinsic temperature reading.

For a thermal emitting surface in local equilibrium, adopt the Planck radiance B_λ(T)=2hc²/[λ⁵(exp(hc/(λk_B T))−1)]. This physical radiation law requires quantum/statistical premises beyond a classical oscillating charge. Here it is an accepted model connected to [Review statistical descriptions with their constraints dynamics and evidence](Review-statistical-descriptions-with-their-constraints-dynamics-and-evidence.lingua#r_0048D075F0EB33EFBEDD46775E) and [Review quantum descriptions with their physical premises and evidence limits](Review-quantum-descriptions-with-their-physical-premises-and-evidence-limits.lingua#r_00CFA9ABD5C9D7D59E8532DC9F), not a claim that their finite-state examples derived the electromagnetic mode density. Integrating the isotropic surface intensity over directions gives flux πB_λ, and integrating wavelengths gives σT⁴. Effective temperature is defined by L=4πR²σT_eff⁴, even when the detailed stellar spectrum is not a perfect blackbody.

The substitution x=hc/(λk_B T) explains the T⁴ scaling. Maximizing B_λ yields x=5(1−e^(−x)) at its positive maximum, giving λ_peak T constant. The numerical constant and total Planck integral can be studied in later radiation formation. A hotter blackbody has a bluer wavelength peak, but dust, unresolved companions, line absorption and detector response can change measured color. Two different intrinsic band pairs (3,1) and (3/2,1) give the same transmitted pair (3/2,1) under transmissions (1/2,1) and (1,1); this is an algebraic spectral ambiguity, not two asserted blackbody temperatures.

Atomic/molecular absorption and emission connect line patterns to allowed energy changes through [Use spectra to connect energy changes with atomic structure](../../chemistry/general-chemistry/atomic/Light-spectra-and-energy-levels.lingua#r_3Z2QB3MQ90C9GRT3XV9QNKN7KG). Line strength also depends on excitation, ionization, optical depth and abundances; absence of a visible line does not establish absence of an element. Broadening combines motion, thermal distribution, pressure, rotation and instrumental effects. Several lines and physical constraints are needed to discriminate explanations.

Define redshift z=(λ_obs−λ_rest)/λ_rest after correcting the observer/reference convention. For pure longitudinal special-relativistic recession, 1+z=√[(1+β)/(1−β)], so β=[(1+z)²−1]/[(1+z)²+1]; for |β|≪1, z≈β. Reuse [Preserve causal order and distinguish clock rates from received frequencies](Preserve-causal-order-and-distinguish-clock-rates-from-received-frequencies.lingua#r_00F4F31E0DC57AC39F51E3B5DA). Gravity and cosmic expansion can also shift spectra; that local velocity inversion is not universal.

**Work:** check the wavelength/frequency Jacobian, compare two equal-temperature stars with different radii, and give an observation that helps separate dust from temperature. Read the selected thermal-radiation passage in 5.2 of [Astronomy second edition by OpenStax](../sources/Astronomy-second-edition-by-OpenStax.lingua#r_00466D09500F8EEF3B1876A23F); chapters 5 and 17 supply the wider progressive spectrum assignment.

